**Friction Points of Movement to Work

* Entry-level jobs requiring previous experience
* Uncertainty around how to create a professional CV
* Lack of confidence and limited interview practice
* Unclear understanding of where to access employment support
* Uncertainty around available work-experience opportunities
* Jobs being difficult to reach using public transport
* Travel costs creating an additional barrier
* Difficulty transitioning from education into employment
* Difficulty recognising or explaining transferable skills to employers
* Limited understanding of AI and how it can be used appropriately during job applications
* Job descriptions requesting specialised skills that users may not currently possess
* No clear understanding of what happens during the two-week programme
* Difficulty finding relevant work experience
* Lack of motivation after repeated unsuccessful applications
* Anxiety around entering an unfamiliar workplace
* Uncertainty about what employers expect from candidates
* Limited knowledge of different job roles and career paths
* Difficulty tailoring applications to specific roles
* Limited access to suitable devices or reliable internet
* Low digital confidence when completing online applications
* Difficulty understanding job adverts and application terminology
* Lack of recent experience to discuss during interviews
* Concern that short-term work experience may not lead to employment
* Not knowing how to present gaps in employment or education
* Limited awareness of local employers and sectors
* Uncertainty around workplace expectations such as punctuality, communication and dress
* Fear of making mistakes or asking questions in a workplace
* Difficulty knowing which skills are most relevant to a specific job
